DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("ln((cos(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln((ln(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("((4, 8)) U (4, 8)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("[0, 5] - ((-infinity, infinity) - [0, 5]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [0, 5])");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("[3, 7] - ((-infinity, infinity) - {7, 8}) U {7, 8}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("([3, 7]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {7, 8}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {7, 8})");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{7, 8} - ((-infinity, infinity) - [3, 7]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ([3, 7] - ((-infinity, infinity) - [3, 7])))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`13.63+19.36-1.03+14`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('45.96')}
---

[`8*6+8.39*18`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('199.02')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 19\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 3 \leq x \leq 7\}`]
- [`C = \{7, 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap C \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(B) \cap C \cap C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`C \cap B \cap (B \cap B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 4 < x < 8\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 0 \leq x \leq 5\}`]

Compute:
- [`(A) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cap B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 1, 1, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 0, -6, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -10, 1, 3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<0, -6, -9>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, -6, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, -6, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, 1, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<0, -6, -9>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 1, 3>") x Compute("<1, 1, 7>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 9, -6, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, -2, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<9, -6, 1>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, -2, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<9, -6, 1>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, -2, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();